   **`messages.json` IS filtered, and this entry records exactly how,
   because the filter is not a suite filter.** Upstream's file is 2 685 714
   bytes: 300 entries, each carrying 17 fields, with NO `cipher_suite` key
   at all (every entry is suite-agnostic), so item 4's
   `select(.cipher_suite==1)` approach does not apply. ONE reduction is
   applied instead — an ENTRY prefix, the first 20 of 300, keeping all 17
   fields:

     jq -c '.[0:20]' messages.json

   The entry cut needs justifying, so: all 300 entries were decoded and
   their structural variants counted before choosing. They are structurally
   IDENTICAL i.i.d. samples — every entry has a `member` sender, an `add`
   proposal in `public_message_proposal`, a Commit with one by-reference
   `ProposalOrRef` and a 1-node `UpdatePath`, an `update` LeafNode with
   source `update`, an `external` PSK type, a `Welcome` with one recipient,
   a `GroupInfo` carrying a `ratchet_tree` and an `external_pub` extension,
   and a `GroupSecrets` with its `path_secret` present and a non-empty PSK
   list. The ONLY field that varies structurally across the file is
   `private_message.content_type`, which takes all three values, and the
   shortest prefix covering all three is 3 entries. 20 was taken rather
   than 3 for margin (all three content types appear 9/5/6 times in it),
   giving 160 830 bytes — the same order as the already-embedded filtered
   `tree-validation.json` (115 KB), against 2.7 MB for the full file.
   `kat_messages_test.zig` ASSERTS the coverage this reasoning rests on
   (all three §6 content types, all five §17.2 wire formats, at least one
   Commit with a path and at least one by-reference proposal, at least one
   `GroupSecrets` with a `path_secret` and at least one with PSKs), so a
   future re-filter that silently lost a variant fails the test rather than
   passing quietly. SHA-256 of the embedded (filtered) file:
   `694d7d5747b143042f97e5a52cb3f0fd919d722c25a509410dba0ad1df0824cb`; of
   the unfiltered upstream file as fetched:
   `b194abe1561995223482dbad51c180146920dc2f637e74d01e07a388308791fb`.

